@baseUrl = http://localhost:5191

### Get all employees
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees

### Get one employee
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/1

### Create an employee (expect 201 Created + Location header)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sara Ahmad",
  "email": "sara@acme.com",
  "position": "Customer Support",
  "team": "Team #1",
  "active": true
}

### Get the employee you just created (use the id from the Location header)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/3

### Get an employee that doesn't exist (should be 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/99

### Update an employee (expect 200 OK)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ali Mohammad",
  "email": "ali.m@acme.com",
  "position": "Senior Developer",
  "team": "IT",
  "active": true
}

### Check the update (email and position should be changed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/1

### Update an employee that doesn't exist (expect 404 Not Found)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/99
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nobody",
  "email": "nobody@acme.com",
  "position": "Developer",
  "team": "IT",
  "active": true
}

### Update with invalid data (expect 400 with validation errors)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "position": "",
  "team": "IT",
  "active": true
}

### Delete an employee (expect 204 No Content)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/2

### Check the delete (expect 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/2

### Delete an employee that doesn't exist (expect 404 Not Found)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/99

### After a delete, create another employee - what id does it get? Is it unique?
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Omar Hassan",
  "email": "omar@acme.com",
  "position": "Technician",
  "team": "Maintenance",
  "active": true
}

### List everyone - look at the ids
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees
